The Terror of Cagley, which the children of Cagley called the Shadow Demon, is a tall, gangly figure made of cut-out darkness, with two pinprick points of white light for eyes. It laired at the bottom of the mine beneath Mount Cagley, near the town of [[Cagley]].

It shows a victim a death that has succeeded, and the fear of it takes root. It can wear the shape of someone its victim dreads: one child saw it become his football coach, telling him he would never make varsity.

A group of Cagley children went down the mine to kill it. It greeted them with "I'm so glad you all came." They destroyed it, and the cavern collapsed behind them. The town is no longer haunted. The creature will reform in thirty years.
